{"availability":"available","full":"facka/tomation","name":"tomation","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2023-08-25T04:38:25Z","updated":"2026-10-12T04:18:13Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://facka.github.io/tomation/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T07:12:43.965Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T07:12:43.965Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T07:12:43.965Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T02:35:51.800Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T09:03:17.448Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T00:54:13.700Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-18T07:12:43.965Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A TypeScript-first browser automation framework that lets you write readable, maintainable UI tests using a declarative DSL — then run them directly in the browser via a lightweight extension.","Tomation separates what you're testing from how elements are found on the page. You declare elements using a tag-based builder pattern, compose reusable tasks, and write tests that read like plain English. The compiler transforms your TypeScript source into a portable .tomation.json file that the browser extension executes step-by-step."],"features":["TypeScript-first — Full editor autocomplete, type safety, and go-to-definition","Declarative element selectors — is.BUTTON.where(idIs('login')).as('Login Button')","XPath support — Element('//div[@role=\"alert\"]').as('Alert')","Reusable tasks — Compose multi-step workflows with parameters and conditionals","Automations — Parameterized test procedures with a runtime form for user-provided values"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/facka/tomation/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"089f8809394640eb455835ec9041322d4167f9ec7937cb0707bd008d27d44dc7","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T02:35:51.947Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T07:12:4